# INTENTIONALLY NO CUSTOM CATCH-ALL RULE HERE. Do not add one back without
# testing it on a Cloudflare Pages preview deployment first.
#
# History (2026-07-21): a custom "/*  /some-target  200" catch-all rule
# was added twice to route non-prerendered paths (checkout, admin,
# admin-created program slugs) to a dedicated fallback shell. Both
# attempts caused a live redirect loop and took swingtheory.golf down —
# first with the target as a bare top-level file ("/spa.html", which
# Cloudflare auto-redirects to its extensionless "/spa", which then
# re-matched the same /* rule and looped), then again with the target as
# a directory form ("/spa/"), which was assumed safe by analogy to how
# root "/" + index.html behaves but turned out not to be — Cloudflare's
# exact resolution order for _redirects rewrite targets vs. its own
# automatic redirects is not something either attempt got right.
#
# Current behavior instead: no matching rule + no top-level 404.html file
# means Cloudflare Pages' own default, documented SPA fallback serves
# root dist/index.html (the prerendered homepage) for any unmatched path,
# with zero custom rewrite logic in the loop. src/main.tsx already
# handles a served page not matching the current URL (its
# prerender-path marker won't equal e.g. "/memberships/checkout") by
# clearing #root and doing a plain client render, so those routes still
# end up correct once JS runs — the only cost is a brief flash of
# homepage content/meta before that happens, which is a UX nit, not a
# broken page. That trade is deliberate: it's the same "single generic
# shell for everything" behavior the pre-prerender site always had for
# these routes, just without the noindex nicety the custom shell added.
